cash-open = Cash outlook
cash-title = Cash outlook — construction and income
cash-close = Close cash outlook
cash-preview = Preview plant
cash-committed = Existing commitments only
cash-cell = Preview construction at ({ $x }, { $y }). Choosing a plant here does not order it.
cash-pick-cell = Select an empty land cell before opening this dialog to preview a new plant's construction payments.
cash-no-history = No completed months yet. Only construction payments are shown; an income estimate becomes available after your first month closes.
cash-history = Operating income from { $count } completed months, before construction: low { $low }, average { $mean }, high { $high } per month at today's tariff.
cash-lowest = Lowest projected average month-end cash: { $cash } in { $month }.
cash-risk = The lower income scenario falls below zero cash in { $month }.
cash-now = Now
cash-baseline = Existing commitments + average income
cash-proposed = With proposed plant + average income
cash-capital-only = Construction payments only
cash-range = Income scenario range
cash-zero = Zero cash
cash-existing-payments = Committed payments
cash-new-payments = Proposed payments
cash-low = Lower cash scenario
cash-mean = Average cash scenario
cash-high = Upper cash scenario
cash-scenarios = The shaded cone repeats the lowest and highest operating results from up to 12 completed months. It is a scenario range, not a confidence interval or a guarantee. One completed month has no historical spread.
cash-operations = Operations stay as observed. Future demand, seasons, reliability, new-plant output and upkeep, and unquoted grid connections are not predicted. A new plant's construction costs are included without assuming extra income from it.
cash-payments = Payments include remaining plant, line, HVDC and makeup-drilling commitments. Geothermal payments assume exploration succeeds. The chart extends through construction, up to 10 years; later payments are outside the chart.
cash-tariff-help = January tariff scenarios use the region's minimum, base and maximum allowed returns, recent operating costs and energy sold, and today's eligible assets as they depreciate. Future commissioning, capital holds and write-offs may change the actual tariff.
cash-tariff-range = From { $month }: tariff scenarios { $low } / { $mean } / { $high }.
cash-unavailable = This cash outlook cannot be calculated for the current construction terms.
